11. Brought services back one at a time with 5-minute waits
12. All services came back cleanly, ZERO new restarts on any
    newly-scheduled pod
13. Cluster is now fully operational and stable

Root cause: CASCADE FAILURE DYNAMICS in the K8s cluster itself.
Not hardware. Not memory. Not a software bug. Not TS-K8S-038.

Mechanism: When the cluster experiences any trigger event (OOM,
probe timeout, brief apiserver unavailability), control plane
components fail liveness probes and restart. Each restart
generates IO load (LIST operations, log writes, image pulls).
On resource-constrained hardware, this load prevents the next
restart from succeeding fast enough to beat ITS liveness probe.
Feedback loop continues indefinitely until external intervention.

