[What We Definitively Know Now]

1. The cluster CAN run all its workloads stably on current hardware
   - Final state showed 3-4% CPU utilization across all nodes
   - Memory at 56-77% (tight but not critical)
   - Everything Running, zero new restarts during reintroduction

2. The cluster CANNOT recover from cascade failures on its own
   - Once in cascade, probe timeouts perpetuate the failure state
   - External intervention (scale to 0, let settle, scale up)
     is required to break the loop

3. Sequential startup is mandatory
   - Parallel startup of 5+ VMs at once causes boot storm
   - Each startup adds load; parallel startups compound the load
   - 60-second delays between VM starts avoids this

4. Sequential workload reintroduction is mandatory
   - Even after baseline is established, bringing up 20+ workloads
     at once will recreate cascade conditions
   - 5-minute delays between workload activations works cleanly

5. The trigger for the initial cascade is unclear
   - Master1's hang earlier today started it
   - But what caused master1 to hang is still unknown
   - Root investigation of THAT requires previous-boot journal review
