[Critical Reminders for Future Incidents]

## When you see PSI sustained >30% for >10 minutes

1. DO NOT reboot VMs — this makes it worse (new boot storm load)
2. DO NOT drain nodes — eviction creates more cascade load
3. DO scale workloads down (apps first, then monitoring, then flux)
4. DO wait 15-20 minutes for baseline
5. DO scale back up one service at a time with 5 min waits

## When you need to make VM changes

1. ALWAYS sequential, never parallel
2. ALWAYS wait for one VM to be fully healthy before touching the next
3. For masters: etcd quorum means 2-of-3 up throughout any change
4. For workers: drain first, don't just shut down

## When GitOps is reverting your changes

1. Suspend the relevant kustomizations BEFORE scaling
   kubectl patch kustomization <name> -n flux-system \
     --type=merge -p '{"spec":{"suspend":true}}'
2. Or shut down flux controllers first
3. Or commit desired state to git FIRST

